meta {
  name: Emails
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  NotificationService has no API for sending mail: each request here publishes a message to a Kafka topic through
  Kafka UI's REST API (`{{kafkaUiUrl}}`, started with the compose stack), and the service emails it.

  Run `make notification GMAIL_PASSWORD=...` (or `make up GMAIL_PASSWORD=...`) first. Set `recipient` in the
  environment to a mailbox you own: these send real email through Gmail. `sender` must be the Gmail account the
  password belongs to, because the service logs in to SMTP as the message's `from`.

  A 200 only means the message reached the topic; whether the email went out is in the service log
  (`.run/notification-1.log`) and the recipient's inbox.
}
